      "writtenOn": "2021-02-09T06:48:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can\u0027t we just pare down the existing driver using CONFIG_* options if we don\u0027t need the host mode? It\u0027s kind of getting out of hand now. There\u0027s already a separate Type-C stack, a separate TCPC driver, and now this. I understand that the  free space is tight, but if it\u0027s possible to leverage the existing drivers, we should do so.",
